The gland in the thorax secretes the hormone ecdysone which induces metamorphosis. This hormone, however, can not initiate metamorphosis unless a second hormone called prothoracicotrophic hormone (PTTH) is present. PTTH is secreted by the brain in the insect's head. Prothoracic glands in the insect's body (the gland in the thoracic segment of the insect) produce ecdysone, so "J" can be a correct answer, but the full process requires both the PTTH signal and the hormone ecdysone. This makes (A) the correct answer.
